    {
      "name": "Health Card",
      "kind": "card",
      "refersTo": "card",
      "description": "The Home hero: last result as a big tabular figure in its state colour, a state square, and the amber Run health check button.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-health\"><div class=\"ds-health-top\"><div class=\"ds-health-text\"><div class=\"ds-health-when\">Last health check, today 12:31</div><div class=\"ds-health-big\"><span class=\"ds-health-n\">8</span><span class=\"ds-health-unit\">faults</span></div><div class=\"ds-health-sub\">Engine light on · 1 emissions test not ready</div></div><div class=\"ds-health-state\"><svg width=\"30\" height=\"30\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"12\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#FF6961\"/><path d=\"M12 7v6M12 16.5v.5\" stroke=\"#1C1C1E\" stroke-width=\"2.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/></svg></div></div><button class=\"ds-health-btn\"><svg width=\"18\" height=\"18\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M12 20s-7-4.4-9-9a4.8 4.8 0 0 1 9-3 4.8 4.8 0 0 1 9 3c-2 4.6-9 9-9 9z\" fill=\"currentColor\"/></svg>Run health check</button><div class=\"ds-health-cap\">Reads 33 control modules and the engine light</div></div>",
      "css": ".ds-health{background:#1C1C1E;border-radius:16px;padding:24px;max-width:390px;font-family:-apple-system, 'SF Pro Text', system-ui, sans-serif;color:#FFFFFF}.ds-health-top{display:flex;gap:12px;align-items:flex-start}.ds-health-text{flex:1}.ds-health-when,.ds-health-cap{font-size:13px;line-height:18px;letter-spacing:-0.08px;color:rgba(235,235,245,0.64)}.ds-health-big{display:flex;align-items:flex-end;gap:8px;margin-top:2px}.ds-health-n{font-size:56px;line-height:62px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-1px;color:#FF6961;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}.ds-health-unit{font-size:20px;line-height:25px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:0.38px;margin-bottom:8px}.ds-health-sub{font-size:15px;line-height:20px;letter-spacing:-0.24px;color:rgba(235,235,245,0.64)}.ds-health-state{width:56px;height:56px;border-radius:16px;background:rgba(255,69,58,0.2);display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center}.ds-health-btn{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;gap:8px;min-height:50px;padding:0 24px;border:none;border-radius:25px;font-family:-apple-system, 'SF Pro Text', system-ui, sans-serif;font-size:17px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:-0.41px;cursor:pointer;transition:transform 0.12s ease-out, opacity 0.12s ease-out;background:#FFB340;color:#1A1205;width:100%;margin-top:24px}.ds-health-btn:hover{opacity:0.9}.ds-health-btn:active{opacity:0.75;transform:scale(0.97)}.ds-health-btn:focus-visible{outline:2px solid #FFB340;outline-offset:3px}.ds-health-btn:disabled{opacity:0.4;cursor:default}.ds-health-cap{text-align:center;margin-top:8px}"
    },
    {
      "name": "ScanPulse",
      "kind": "custom",
      "refersTo": "accent",
      "description": "Signature: amber rings ripple out from the car symbol while the car is read, over a tabular percentage; still under Reduce Motion.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-scan\"><div class=\"ds-scan-pulse\"><span class=\"ds-ring\"></span><span class=\"ds-ring\"></span><span class=\"ds-ring\"></span><span class=\"ds-scan-core\"><svg width=\"34\" height=\"34\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M3 15v-3l2-4.5A2 2 0 0 1 6.8 6h10.4a2 2 0 0 1 1.8 1.5L21 12v3h-2a2 2 0 0 1-4 0H9a2 2 0 0 1-4 0z\" fill=\"currentColor\"/></svg></span></div><div class=\"ds-scan-pct\">42%</div><div class=\"ds-scan-sub\">Reading Airbag…</div></div>",
      "css": ".ds-scan{display:flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:center;background:#1C1C1E;border-radius:16px;padding:24px;max-width:390px;font-family:-apple-system, 'SF Pro Text', system-ui, sans-serif}.ds-scan-pulse{position:relative;width:132px;height:132px;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center}.ds-ring{position:absolute;width:74px;height:74px;border-radius:50%;border:2px solid #FFB340;opacity:0;animation:ds-ripple 1800ms cubic-bezier(0.33,1,0.68,1) infinite}.ds-ring:nth-child(2){animation-delay:600ms}.ds-ring:nth-child(3){animation-delay:1200ms}.ds-scan-core{position:relative;width:74px;height:74px;border-radius:50%;background:rgba(255,179,64,0.18);color:#FFB340;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center}.ds-scan-pct{font-size:34px;line-height:41px;font-weight:700;color:#FFFFFF;margin-top:8px;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}.ds-scan-sub{font-size:15px;line-height:20px;letter-spacing:-0.24px;color:rgba(235,235,245,0.64)}@keyframes ds-ripple{0%{opacity:0;transform:scale(1)}20%{opacity:0.55}100%{opacity:0;transform:scale(1.78)}}@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce){.ds-ring{animation:none;opacity:0}}"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Driver's Seat at Night",
    "overview": "Caristini is a first-party iOS app, used in a dark car with the ignition on and the phone in one hand. The world is iOS itself, executed at the craft level of Apple's own apps: a true black ground, grouped secondary surfaces, hairline separators, San Francisco at Dynamic Type sizes, SF Symbols, a native glass tab bar and large titles that collapse into the system bar material. Dark appearance is the default scene; light appearance is a full alternative built from the same token names.\n\nColour is spent on meaning. One amber tint marks everything you can tap. System red and green say fault and healthy. Each tool owns one coloured rounded square, as in iOS Settings. Everything else is neutral grey on black, so a result reads at a glance to someone who is not technical.\n\nMotion is reserved for the car talking back: rings ripple out from the car symbol while a scan runs, and each module's result slides up as it answers. Both stop under Reduce Motion.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "True black ground (`bg`), grouped secondary surfaces (`surface`), hairline `border` separators.",
      "One amber tint (`accent` and `accentText`) for interactive elements.",
      "State colours carry meaning: `danger` for faults, `ok` for healthy, neutral grey for everything non-urgent.",
      "One fixed colour square per tool, white SF Symbol glyph.",
      "Inset grouped sections with uppercase headers outside the container.",
      "Tabular figures for every number; Menlo for codes.",
      "Native chrome: glass tab bar, large-title stacks, blur header, system action sheets."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The One Tint Rule",
        "body": "Amber marks what you can tap: buttons, bar buttons, the selected tab, checkmarks, the cursor. The one sanctioned non-interactive use is progress of an action the user started (ScanPulse rings and ProgressBar fill). Nothing else is amber.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Meaning Rule",
        "body": "Red means a fault or a destructive action. Green means healthy. Anything non-urgent (could not read, minor, not found) is neutral grey on `sunken`. Red and green are never decoration.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The One Square Rule",
        "body": "Each tool owns one colour square, everywhere it appears. A row may switch its square to `red` or `green` to report state (a faulty module, a low battery); it never borrows another tool's colour.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Tabular Rule",
        "body": "Every number uses tabular figures (`type.number`, which sets `tabular-nums`), so counts, percentages, voltages and live values hold their width while they change.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Dynamic Type Rule",
        "body": "Text sizes come from `type` in `src/theme.ts`. Off-scale sizes are drift.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Tonal Depth Rule",
        "body": "Lift is a step in the grey ladder, never a shadow.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** use `accent` and `accentText` for every tappable element and nothing else, except ScanPulse and ProgressBar progress.",
      "**Do** colour a result by meaning: `danger` for faults, `ok` for healthy, neutral `sunken` with `muted` for non-urgent states.",
      "**Do** keep each tool on its own square: Diagnose `red`, Live data `blue`, Service `green`, ECU info `indigo`, Customise `purple`, Code lookup `teal`.",
      "**Do** build screens from inset grouped sections with the uppercase header outside the container.",
      "**Do** set every number with tabular figures and every code or VIN in Menlo.",
      "**Do** honour Reduce Motion in any new motion, as ScanPulse and Arrive do.",
      "**Do** put every write to the car behind the Confirm Sheet (the system action sheet on iPhone), stating ignition state and consequence.",
      "**Do** keep demo cars behind `Platform.OS === 'web'`; the phone app connects to real adapters only."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** use amber for decoration, headings, illustrations or status.",
      "**Don't** use red or green for a state that is not a fault or a healthy result; minor and unknown stay grey.",
      "**Don't** give a non-tool row a tool's colour square.",
      "**Don't** add shadows; depth is tonal.",
      "**Don't** set text sizes outside the `type` scale.",
      "**Don't** replace native chrome (tab bar, headers, action sheets) with drawn imitations on iPhone."
    ]
  }
}
